\paragraph{From diagnosis to practice.}\label{sec:selection_method}\label{sec:conclusion}
Entity-level construction bypasses both failure mechanisms when degeneracy ${<}22$\% ($p{<}0.01$; Appendix~\ref{app:epoch_confound}); LP compression (median 0.041 nats) connects to calibration challenges \cite{kadavath2022language, xiong2024verbalized}.
We position these gains ($+0.3$--$1.4$\,pp at $N{\times}$ inference cost) as diagnostic evidence: aggregation fails above $\theta_{\text{crit}}{=}0.70$, and a major contributing factor is near-zero selection alignment ($\alpha{\to}0$) even when $\rho$ is substantial.
